        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Madurai</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 300 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">The city's recorded history is dated to the 3rd century BCE, and the Sangam period settlement site of Keeladi nearby dates to the 6th century BCE.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the banks of the Vaigai River, on a flat and fertile plain south-east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-ghats">Western Ghats</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandyas</a>; the Tamil Sangam, said to have been held there; the Meenakshi and Koodal Azhagar temples; the concentric streets laid out under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayaks</a>; the sieges of 1763 and 1764; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Gandhi</a>'s adoption of the loin cloth in 1921; the temple entry movement of 1939</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Madurai is a major city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a> and the administrative headquarters of Madurai district.</span></div>
